// Structure for requesting constructive feedback after rejection
// Subject: Request for Interview Feedback - [Your Name]

Dear [Interviewer/Recruiter Name],

Thank you for considering me for the Java Backend Developer position.
While I'm disappointed I won't be joining the team, I appreciate the time
you invested in the interview process.

// Direct, humble request
If possible, I'd be grateful for any feedback on areas where I could improve.
Specifically, if there were technical concepts or communication skills
that I should focus on, that guidance would be valuable for my growth.

// Professional close without pressure
I understand you're busy, so even brief feedback would be helpful.
I hope our paths cross again in the future.

Best regards,
[Your Name]

// Key points:
// - Keep it under 100 words
// - Don't argue or ask them to reconsider
// - Make it easy for them to give one-line feedback
// - Show you're focused on growth, not dwelling on the rejection

// Not executable code, but a structured approach to your first week

record FirstWeekChecklist(
    List<String> techStackItems,
    List<String> codereviewGoals,
    List<String> relationshipGoals
) {}

var weekOneGoals = new FirstWeekChecklist(
    List.of(
        "Set up local dev environment and run the main service",
        "Clone all relevant repositories and understand project structure",
        "Read architecture documentation and draw a system diagram",
        "Identify the three most frequently modified modules",
        "Understand deployment process and CI/CD pipeline"
    ),
    List.of(
        "Read 10-15 recent pull requests to understand code review culture",
        "Note common feedback patterns from senior developers",
        "Understand team's coding standards and naming conventions",
        "Review how they write tests and what coverage they expect"
    ),
    List.of(
        "Schedule 1-on-1 coffee chats with each team member",
        "Ask teammates what they wish they'd known in their first month",
        "Identify who to ask about specific domains: DB, deployment, APIs"
    )
);
